WEBVTT

00:00:02.108 --> 00:00:05.426
<v><b>Doctor:</b></v> When was it she last walked?

00:00:05.827 --> 00:00:07.199
<v><b>Gentlewoman:</b></v> For two nights together,

00:00:07.226 --> 00:00:12.408
I have seen her rise from her bed, throw her nightgown upon her, unlock her closet,

00:00:12.541 --> 00:00:19.105
<b>take forth</b> paper, fold it, write upon it, read it, afterwards seal it, and again return to bed;

00:00:19.132 --> 00:00:21.778
yet all this while in a most fast sleep.

00:00:21.865 --> 00:00:26.540
<v><b>Doctor:</b></v> Besides her walking and other actual performances,

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:30.954
what, at any time, have you heard her say?

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:33.478
<v><b>Gentlewoman:</b></v> That, which I will not report after her.

00:00:33.525 --> 00:00:36.905
<v><b>Doctor:</b></v> You may to me and ‘tis most meet you should.

00:00:36.944 --> 00:00:40.746
<v><b>Gentlewoman:</b></v> Neither to you, nor any one, having no witness to confirm my speech.

00:00:40.819 --> 00:00:51.271
<b>Lo you</b>, here she comes − this is her very <b>guise</b>, and, upon my life, fast asleep.

00:00:51.565 --> 00:00:53.257
Observe her and stand close.

00:00:53.304 --> 00:00:54.726
<v><b>Doctor:</b></v> How came she by that light?

00:00:54.751 --> 00:00:58.236
<v><b>Gentlewoman:</b></v> She has light by her, continually, ‘tis her command.

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:10.998
<v><b>Doctor:</b></v> You see her eyes are open.

00:01:11.138 --> 00:01:13.886
<v><b>Gentlewoman:</b></v> Aye, but their sense is shut.

00:01:23.206 --> 00:01:24.746
<v><b>Doctor:</b></v> What is it she does now?

00:01:24.786 --> 00:01:26.785
<v><b>Gentlewoman:</b></v> It is an accustomed action with her.

00:01:27.151 --> 00:01:30.975
<v><b>Lady Macbeth:</b></v> Yet here’s a spot.

00:01:37.679 --> 00:01:43.433
Out, damned spot − out, I say.

00:01:43.753 --> 00:01:55.239
One − two − why, then, ’tis time to do it − Hell is murky.

00:01:56.663 --> 00:02:01.837
Fie, my lord, fie, a soldier, and <b>afeard</b>?

00:02:03.310 --> 00:02:10.143
What need we fear who knows this, when none can call our power to account?

00:02:12.227 --> 00:02:17.862
Yet who would have thought the old man to have had so much blood in him?

00:02:18.314 --> 00:02:19.485
<v><b>Doctor:</b></v> Do you mark that?

00:02:25.001 --> 00:02:36.380
<v><b>Lady Macbeth:</b></v> The Thane of Fife had a wife − where is she now?

00:02:43.128 --> 00:02:51.422
What, will these hands ne’er be clean?

00:02:53.466 --> 00:02:59.224
No more o’ that, my lord, no more o’ that − you mar all with this starting.

00:02:59.364 --> 00:03:02.667
<v><b>Doctor:</b></v> Go to, go to: you have known what you should not.

00:03:02.734 --> 00:03:06.901
<v><b>Gentleman:</b></v> She has spoke what she should not, I am sure of that.

00:03:08.748 --> 00:03:11.245
<v><b>Lady Macbeth:</b></v> Here’s the smell of the blood still

00:03:14.795 --> 00:03:23.331
− all the perfumes of Arabia will not sweeten this little hand. Oh, oh, oh!

00:03:23.904 --> 00:03:28.538
<v><b>Doctor:</b></v> What a sigh is there. The heart is <b>sorely charged</b>.

00:03:28.563 --> 00:03:32.599
<v><b>Gentlewoman:</b></v> I would not have such a heart in my <b>bosom</b>, for the dignity of the whole body.

00:03:32.633 --> 00:03:36.518
<v><b>Doctor:</b></v> This disease is <b>beyond my practice</b>;

00:03:37.451 --> 00:03:42.419
yet I have known those which have walked in their sleep, who have died holily in their beds.

00:03:42.445 --> 00:03:49.088
<v><b>Lady Macbeth:</b></v> Wash your hands, put on your nightgown, look not so pale:

00:03:50.168 --> 00:03:55.000
I tell you yet again, Banquo’s buried;

00:03:58.447 --> 00:04:00.871
he cannot come out on’s grave.

00:04:01.544 --> 00:04:02.492
<v><b>Doctor:</b></v> Even so?

00:04:02.586 --> 00:04:06.508
<v><b>Lady Macbeth:</b></v> To bed, to bed − there’s knocking at the gate − come,

00:04:10.568 --> 00:04:11.108
come,

00:04:15.425 --> 00:04:16.098
come,

00:04:19.425 --> 00:04:19.865
come.

00:04:28.308 --> 00:04:29.390
Give me your hand.

00:04:33.506 --> 00:04:38.076
What’s done cannot be undone.

00:04:41.883 --> 00:04:42.623
To bed,

00:04:50.021 --> 00:04:50.654
to bed,

00:04:56.323 --> 00:04:57.236
to bed!

00:05:02.368 --> 00:05:05.507
<v><b>Doctor:</b></v> Foul whisperings are abroad.

00:05:06.147 --> 00:05:10.355
Unnatural deeds do breed unnatural troubles:

00:05:10.594 --> 00:05:17.089
infected minds to their deaf pillows will discharge their secrets.

00:05:17.342 --> 00:05:24.955
More needs she the divine than the physician − God, God forgive us all.

00:05:27.075 --> 00:05:33.593
Look after her, remove from her the means of all annoyance, and still keep eyes upon her.

00:05:33.666 --> 00:05:39.291
So, good night, my mind she has <b>mated</b>, and amazed my sight.

00:05:39.745 --> 00:05:43.335
I think, but dare not speak.

00:05:44.061 --> 00:05:45.631
<v><b>Gentlewoman:</b></v> Good night, good doctor.